From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sm6115: source the MDSS AHB clock from the
 active-only XO

The DSI PHY driver hands its "iface" clock to the PM clock framework
(pm_clk_add(), since 6ab502bc1cf3 "drm/msm/dsi: Enable runtime PM"),
which prepares a clock when it is added and only disables it at runtime
suspend. On SM6115 that clock is disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk, so its source
stays prepared for as long as the PHY is bound, and through it the
two-set XO of the RPM: an XO vote in the APSS sleep set with the display
off, which keeps the RPM from shutting XO down in suspend.

Give the display clock controller a second XO input, the active-only
one, and source disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk_src from it, as dispcc-qcm2290 does
for the same clock of the sibling SoC. The other display sources (the
PLL and the MDP, rotator, escape and vsync clocks) stay on the two-set
XO, so a lit display still holds XO while the APSS sleeps and lets it go
when it is off.

The new input is the sixth clock of the node. A device tree with only
five keeps the two-set XO for this source.

The vendor has this source on the two-set XO too (dispcc-bengal.c
disp_cc_parent_names_3; only disp_cc_xo_clk_src is on bi_tcxo_ao). There
the display driver unprepares its clocks when the display goes off
(sde_io_util.c msm_dss_enable_clk()), which mainline's PHY has not done
since the commit above.

Read on the MANGMI Air X, 7.3.5, display off: disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk_src
was the one prepared child left under the two-set XO (prepare 1, enable
0), and the RPM counted an APSS shutdown per suspend but no XO shutdown.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm6115-dispcc.yaml    | 2 ++
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm6115.c                         | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm6115-dispcc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm6115-dispcc.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm6115-dispcc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm6115-dispcc.yaml
@@ -21,12 +21,14 @@
       - qcom,sm6115-dispcc
 
   clocks:
+    minItems: 5
     items:
       - description: Board XO source
       - description: Board sleep clock
       - description: Byte clock from DSI PHY0
       - description: Pixel clock from DSI PHY0
       - description: GPLL0 DISP DIV clock from GCC
+      - description: Board active-only XO source
 
 required:
   - compatible
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm6115.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm6115.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm6115.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm6115.c
@@ -29,10 +29,12 @@
 	DT_DSI0_PHY_PLL_OUT_BYTECLK,
 	DT_DSI0_PHY_PLL_OUT_DSICLK,
 	DT_GPLL0_DISP_DIV,
+	DT_BI_TCXO_AO,
 };
 
 enum {
 	P_BI_TCXO,
+	P_BI_TCXO_AO,
 	P_DISP_CC_PLL0_OUT_MAIN,
 	P_DSI0_PHY_PLL_OUT_BYTECLK,
 	P_DSI0_PHY_PLL_OUT_DSICLK,
@@ -111,12 +113,13 @@
 };
 
 static const struct parent_map disp_cc_parent_map_2[] = {
-	{ P_BI_TCXO, 0 },
+	{ P_BI_TCXO_AO, 0 },
 	{ P_GPLL0_OUT_MAIN, 4 },
 };
 
+/* A device tree without the active-only XO gets the two-set one, as before */
 static const struct clk_parent_data disp_cc_parent_data_2[] = {
-	{ .index = DT_BI_TCXO },
+	{ .index = DT_BI_TCXO_AO, .name = "bi_tcxo" },
 	{ .index = DT_GPLL0_DISP_DIV },
 };
 
@@ -178,7 +181,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk_src[] = {
-	F(19200000, P_BI_TCXO, 1, 0, 0),
+	F(19200000, P_BI_TCXO_AO, 1, 0, 0),
 	F(37500000, P_GPLL0_OUT_MAIN, 8, 0, 0),
 	F(75000000, P_GPLL0_OUT_MAIN, 4, 0, 0),
 	{ }
